{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791698371,"nonce":"wFdogNjU1xsi+ue6L5HelTWqWnU=","title":"Knobs fly in when a panel is shown again after display none","message":"Switching a wiki example between its Preview and Source tabs and back drew the switch knobs sweeping in from the left for about a dozen frames.\n\nCause: a node under `display: none` is laid out as a box with a place and no size. Layout animation kept that box as the node's last layout, so the node came back as a move from it.\n\nReproduced with the wiki driver: go to Source, settle, go back to Preview, and read the knob's drawn position every frame. A quick return (before the hidden layout was settled) did not show it, which is why it looked intermittent.\n\nFix: Flip::laid_out treats a box with no width and no height as not laid out; what appears from one, or goes into one, does so where it is. A box that is shown moves as before.\n\nTests: tests/native-motion.mjs (hidden and shown again, then moved) and adapters/test/wiki.mjs (knobs at rest on every frame after returning from Source, two rounds). Both fail with the rule removed.","files":null}]}